  hint:{en:'Ambivalence is audible. A conceded point is spoken faster and flatter; the reservation after the dash gets a fresh start, slightly lower and slower. Stretching a vowel — “naa-türlich” — marks irony, and overusing it makes every judgement sound insincere.'},
